# Concept
---
Leveraging the concept [here](https://github.com/benjaminsampica) visitors that are signed in can create a digitized card that will be displayed on the profile. This card will be build with the following features:
1. a PRNG seed will be created using the most recent commit from across all repositories \[ref#1\]
  - the back of the card will display a procgen of one of the following
    - maze
    - mondrian \[elements#1\]
    - \*phase2: [book?](https://www.reddit.com/r/proceduralgeneration/comments/os05xs/i_think_i_went_overboard_with_the_procedural_book/)
    - \*phase2: [flags?](https://www.reddit.com/r/proceduralgeneration/comments/yci0yq/some_flags_my_bot_made/)
  - the choice of what to make will be determined by a hash of the username
  - the design will be based off of the procgen
1. the front of the card will have
  - a \(maybe stylized?\) version of the user's avatar
  - the username
  - stats of the user at that (point in time | for phase 1 at least) - derived from the [github readme stats](https://github.com/anuraghazra/github-readme-stats)
> A fun phase 2 of this would be to allow the cards to "battle" based on the user's statistics.
> - by making the stats dynamic and generated at "battle time" users could _level up_ by creating / contributing to their repos
> In this phase we should also show CQRS with rdbms/graphdb/aggregate
>

